meta {
  name: Send WhatsApp template
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/gupshup/test/whatsapp/template
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "phoneNumber": "{{process.env.GUPSHUP_TEST_PHONE}}",
    "templateName": "driver_dl_expiry",
    "parameters": {
      "1": "TS0120200001234",
      "2": "Test Driver",
      "3": "9999999999",
      "4": "7"
    }
  }
}

docs {
  Sends a template (HSM) message through `GupshupWhatsappClient.sendTemplateMessage`
  (VAHN_ADMIN only).

  - `templateName` is a key of `TEMPLATE_CATALOG` in `GupshupWhatsappClient`, for example
    `auth_otp`, `send_otp`, `truck_document_expiry`, `eway_bill_expiry`, `driver_dl_expiry`,
    `tripsheet_resolved`, `iocl_pin_notification`, `new_user_2`, `fund_manager_added`,
    `truck_manager_added_by_torg`, `driver_license_alert`, `truck_document_alert`.
    Unknown names fall back to `templateMapping` in config and are sent with a placeholder body.
  - `parameters` are positional, keyed `"1"`, `"2"`, ... and are substituted into `{{n}}` in the
    body. For OTP templates, `"1"` is also sent as the button URL suffix.

  The example is `driver_dl_expiry`: DL number, driver name, driver phone, days to expiry.
}
